From: Mamuthka linux
Subject: [PATCH] debug-snapshot: do not spin forever after panic when PANIC_REBOOT is off

With CONFIG_DEBUG_SNAPSHOT_PANIC_REBOOT disabled, dbg_snapshot_post_panic()
still parked the CPU in a wfi loop ("for stall cpu when not enabling panic
reboot"), so the phone hung on a kernel panic and PANIC_TIMEOUT never ran.
Return instead, so the stock panic() path flushes the console, waits
PANIC_TIMEOUT seconds (the message stays readable on the display) and then
restarts.

---
diff --git a/lib/debug-snapshot-helper.c b/lib/debug-snapshot-helper.c
index ad5408138..1fff5a601 100644
--- a/lib/debug-snapshot-helper.c
+++ b/lib/debug-snapshot-helper.c
@@ -323,6 +323,16 @@ int dbg_snapshot_post_panic(void)
 
 	dss_soc_ops->soc_post_panic_exit(NULL);
 
+#ifndef CONFIG_DEBUG_SNAPSHOT_PANIC_REBOOT
+	/*
+	 * Without forced reboot, let panic() continue normally: flush the
+	 * console (the panic text stays readable on the screen), wait
+	 * CONFIG_PANIC_TIMEOUT seconds, then emergency_restart().  The
+	 * original code spins here forever (for JTAG ramdump).
+	 */
+	return 0;
+#endif
+
 	/* for stall cpu when not enabling panic reboot */
 	dbg_snapshot_spin_func();
 
